comments:
Looks like a bug of `magic-string` that shouldn't be fixed in Vite? See example:
```js
const s = new MagicString('abc');
s.appendRight(1, 'x');
s.remove(1, 2);
console.log(s.toString()); // ac
```
```js
const s = new MagicString('abc');
s.remove(1, 2);
s.appendRight(1, 'x');
console.log(s.toString()); // axc
```
The same operation in a different order leads to different results.

I spent a while in the debugger tracing this before I found this existing GH issue. I'm pretty sure `magic-string` is doing exactly what is asked of it. MagicString thinks in terms of chunks, plus prefixes and suffixes to those chunks. `appendRight()` adds a prefix to the chunk to the right of (after) the specified position. When we then `remove()` that right-side chunk (in preparation for replacing it with new generated code), MagicString intentionally discards any prefix or suffix as well.

Annotated example:
```ts
// Creates a single chunk to start
const s = new MagicString('abc');

// Cuts it into two chunks: ['a', 'bc'], then attaches 'x' to the right of the
// cutpoint, i.e. prefixes the 'bc' chunk:
s.appendRight(1, 'x'); // yields ['a', (x)'bc'] ==> serializes as 'axbc'

// Positions are relative to original string so this first cuts the second
// chunk, yielding ['a', (x)'b', 'c'], and then clears that middle chunk and all
// of its accessories:
s.remove(1, 2); // ['a', '', 'c'] ==> 'ac'

// We can still append to the left or to the right of those outpoints, even if
// the right side has been "removed" (cleared):
s.appendRight(1, 'y'); // ['a', (y)'', 'c'] ==> 'ayc'

// And the difference between append and prepend is how the two addendums end up
// ordered:
s.appendLeft(2, 'e'); // ['a', (y)''(e), 'c'] ==> 'ayec'
s.prependLeft(2, 'd'); // [a', (y)''(de), 'c'] ==> 'aydec'
s.appendLeft(2, 'f'); // [a', (y)''(def), 'c'] ==> 'aydefc'
```

So anyway in this `ssrTransform()` codepath, Vite is in the process of building up a replacement for the ES6 import/export to the "left" (which was _previously_ `remove()`d to clear it of the original code) so we want a `...Left()` method, not a `...Right()`. Since we've already attached the replacement `import()` and the pseudo-export should logically go after that, we want to append. So `s.appendLeft()` is correct.

TL;DR: No bug in `magic-string`, and Vite should indeed be using `s.appendLeft()`. :) Will comment on PR #6407 as well; I think it is changing too many things at the moment.
